Atlas overlay patch 0054: ui/firstrun-handler
Why: finishing the first-run page has to do things: write Do Not Track, Global Privacy Control and
the tracker-blocker choice, record that the first run is over, make Atlas the default browser when
asked, and open the new tab page or the import page. The page talks to the settings page's own
default-browser handler for the system call (no new code for it) and to the new handler of
components/atlas_pages/setup/ for the rest, in place of the handlers of the upstream setup
bundle. The tracker blocker is a built-in component whose disable state the engine clears at every
start, so switching it off for good is a profile preference read where the component is added
(one early return) plus an unload now. A first-run preference cannot do this: it runs after the
person chooses.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/webui/onboarding/onboarding_page_ui.cc, chrome/browser/extensions/component_loader.cc
Test filter: *AtlasFirstRun*; reel-check scene R04 (choices written; blocker off survives a restart)
Rebase risk: M (the component loader function is added by the inherited blocker patch; the page file by the inherited onboarding patch)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited, platform and 0010 patches applied

